The diagram shows the network of cables that transport high speed internet broadband from a source to a sink.

Each cables' capacity in Mbps is shown.

\exfigure{3313_q13_1}

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{500_q11_s1}

For the maximum flow to be 40, the minimum cut must be 40.

The cut shown has capacity 35, so the maximum flow must be less than 40.

\exfigure{850_q35_s1}

All other cuts are above 23 in value, so the minimum cut is the one shown above. By the max-flow min-cut theorem, its value equals the maximum flow.
$$\begin{aligned}20+x&=23\\ \therefore x&=3\end{aligned}$$

